<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Dictionary</h1>
<p>Usage (while you carry the dictionary):
</p>
<pre>claim dictionary              make it yours, once
alias                         list your aliases
alias &lt;name&gt; &lt;commands&gt;       make an alias
unalias &lt;name&gt; [&lt;name&gt; ...]    remove one or more
</pre>
<p>A dictionary holds aliases: short words that stand for longer commands, or 
for several commands at once. It is the old way to make aliases, and it 
works in any telnet client; the web client has aliases of its own built in 
(see <a cmd='#'>Help Alias</a>). Dictionaries are sold in shops in Udgaard, Midgaard and 
elsewhere.
</p><p>Before its aliases work, claim the dictionary (see <a cmd='#'>Help Claim</a>); after 
that, its aliases work only for you. An alias name can be at most 10 
letters long. Your aliases are kept in the dictionary itself: carry it with 
you, and don't lose it.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Alias</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Claim</a>
</pre>




</div>